  Third-party components used by the build (downloaded or cloned by the scripts, not redistributed here):

  - Filament by Google (Apache-2.0), including the third-party libraries its build brings in (SDL2 (zlib),
    Dear ImGui (MIT), stb (MIT / public domain), Draco, meshoptimizer, Basis Universal, zstd, Abseil and others,
    see its third_party/ directory): the demo renderer. third_party/filament.patch is a modification of Filament's
    sources and is offered under the same Apache-2.0 license; demo/native_window_cocoa.mm follows Filament's
    sample framework.
  - volk (MIT), Vulkan-Headers (Apache-2.0 / MIT), glslang (BSD-3-Clause and others), CMake (BSD-3-Clause),
    Ninja (Apache-2.0): the toolchain under tools/.
  - meshoptimizer (MIT), @gltf-transform (MIT), draco3dgltf (Apache-2.0), Pillow (HPND): the optional scene
    conversion scripts.
  - No scene assets are included. The "Lone Monk" scene (Carlo Bergonzini, CC BY) is referenced by a camera view
    file only.

None of the upstream third-party build components listed above are used or redistributed by three-dlss-nr.
The upstream repository is included as a git submodule (reference/OpenDLSS-NR) for parity testing; the repository
itself is not part of the published three-dlss-nr package. One exception: the optional entry point
`three-dlss-nr/reference-backend` redistributes the MIT-licensed JavaScript and WGSL of the upstream WebGPU port
(ports/browser-webgpu, commit 9d08f4184bbcb9d858e2fb7a7834ec0837a9d2f1), copied unmodified at build time into
vendor/opendlss-nr/ with upstream's LICENSE (Copyright (c) 2026 maan) and a per-file provenance list (SOURCE.json).

